words.mail-pin-body:
Somebody asked for a new PIN on your {brand} account{byHandle}.

Your new PIN is {pin}

Sign in with {signInWith} and this PIN. It works for a day; your old PIN keeps working too until you use this one. Change it under Settings → Signing in.

Or open this link to sign in with it straight away — it works even if wrong PINs have locked the account:

{link}

If this was not you, do nothing — your PIN has not changed, and whoever asked cannot read this email.

words.mail-pin-kid-body:
{first}{handleSaid} has no email of their own and asked for a new PIN.

The new PIN is {pin}

Pass it on to them. They sign in with their handle and this PIN; it works for a day, and their old PIN keeps working until they use this one. "New PIN" on their card in the people column gives a fresh one at once.

Or open this link on their device to sign them in as {who} straight away:

{link}

If they did not ask, do nothing — nothing has changed.
